Area dosimetry or fluence mapping

The formal implementation uses:

Thermoluminescent dosimeter (TLD) arrays — flat sheets of TLD material placed against the body surface, read out after exposure to give a 2D map of dose distribution.

Film dosimetry — radiographic film exposed across a surface area, developed to show dose distribution spatially.

