You made a specific biological observation that is medically precise:

A high dose to a small area vs the same dose spread over a large area produces different biological outcomes.

This is formally captured in radiation medicine as:

Volume effect — the relationship between irradiated volume and biological response.

For a small volume receiving high dose:

    The damage is concentrated
    Surrounding unirradiated tissue provides repair signals from all sides
    Vascular supply from outside the field supports healing
    Recovery is possible because the damage has a border

For a large volume receiving the same total dose:

    Damage is distributed
    No unirradiated tissue reservoir to drive repair from within the field
